T*
() Tj
T*
(Home) Tj
T*
(Dinner guides Easy Sheet-Pan Dinners: One Pan, Almost No Cleanup) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Easy Sheet-Pan Dinners: One Pan, Almost No Cleanup) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(By the Trillion Man Outreach kitchen crew Updated October 8, 2026) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Sheet-pan dinners are the closest thing to a weeknight cheat code. Everything cooks) Tj
T*
(together, the oven does the work and a layer of foil means there is nothing to scrub) Tj
T*
(afterward. Here is the simple formula, the timing rules that keep everything from) Tj
T*
(burning or going soggy, and five combinations to start with.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The sheet-pan formula) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Pick one protein, one or two vegetables and a starch. Toss with oil, salt and a) Tj
T*
(seasoning, spread in a single layer and roast at 425 F. That is the whole method.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Protein:) Tj
T*
(fully cooked sausage, chicken thighs or strips, shrimp, salmon, tofu or chickpeas.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Vegetables:) Tj
T*
(broccoli, bell peppers, zucchini, green beans, carrots, brussels sprouts.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Starch:) Tj
T*
(baby potatoes, sweet potato cubes, or serve everything over rice, tortillas or pasta.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Flavor:) Tj
T*
(garlic powder, taco seasoning, Italian seasoning, smoked paprika or a spoonful of pesto) Tj
T*
(after roasting.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Timing rules that prevent soggy or burnt food) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Start slow foods first.) Tj
T*
(Potatoes need about 10 minutes of head start before broccoli and sausage go on.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Cut to match.) Tj
T*
(Small pieces cook faster. Cut dense vegetables smaller than soft ones.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Do not crowd the pan.) Tj
T*
(Crowded food steams instead of roasts. Use two pans if needed.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Line with foil.) Tj
T*
(It saves cleanup. For extra browning, preheat the pan.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Check doneness.) Tj
T*
(Chicken should reach 165 F. Check the) Tj
T*
(USDA temperature chart) Tj
T*
ET

